        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(supervisor): suppress unhandled stream errors on child stdout/stderr",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where a supervised child process could crash OpenClaw if stdout or stderr emitted an error after spawn but before the supervisor registered output subscribers.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe child adapter now installs exactly one stream-lifetime error guard on stdout and stderr during adapter construction. Subscriber registration remains responsible only for decoding data; existing stream `close` handlers continue to own decoder flush and Windows drain completion.\n\n## User Impact\n\nEarly child output-stream failures no longer escape as unhandled Node `error` events. Repeated output subscriptions do not accumulate redundant permanent error listeners, and process wait behavior remains unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/process/supervisor/adapters/child.test.ts` (19 passed).\n- The test emits errors before output registration, verifies one listener after repeated subscriptions, and proves Windows `wait()` settles only after stream close.\n- Real Node child-pipe probe confirmed a destroyed output source emits `error` then `close`.\n- `oxfmt` and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh structured autoreview reported no accepted or actionable findings.\n- Exact prepared head: `a968528d469c3b4e1ca1b7701b84854d9f92160b`.\n",
